<!--
The single canonical entry for the beet website: the content Router serving the
`routes/` directory, every page wrapped in `templates/Layout.bsx`. Discovery loads
it locally when the `beet` binary runs from the `site/` directory (`cd site && beet
serve`, and `beet present`, `beet check`, `beet export-static`), and the deployed
Lightsail box loads the same entry directly from the app bucket root. Either way
this entry's `StartOnLoad` root carries the servers, and its `CallOnLoad` fires
once the build loads, fanning the request out to them.

It declares the three long-running servers (`HttpServer`, the local live
`TuiServer`, and the multi-tenant `SshTuiServer`), so `--server` picks them once
booted: the default boots them all, `--server=http,ssh` serves html over http and
a live terminal over ssh, `--server=tui` runs the local `beet present` terminal. It
carries no `CliServer` (a one-shot would resolve the boot and exit), so the boot
parks on the servers' keep-alive and the serve-feature binary stays up. Each server
dispatches down into the `Router` child.

The router's middleware and the layout attach as component spreads (request
logging, `--help`, terminal link navigation, the layout, and the cache policy:
`CacheHeadersMiddleware` + `CacheHeaders` mark html pages edge-cacheable, which
the Cloudflare proxy honors and the deploy/sync purge refreshes).
`<DefaultAppRoutes/>` adds the default app routes (`/app-info`, the reactivity
runtime, …), `<RoutesDir/>` discovers the `routes/` pages, and `<AssetsDir
src="assets" cache="1h"/>` mounts the assets the site and blog reference (the
favicon, images), browser-cacheable for an hour. It is one plain subdir of the
site store: in dev `site/assets` is a committed symlink to the workspace
`assets/` (hydrated by `just beet-shared pull`), and the deploy replicates it
into the app bucket, so the store path is the same either side. `<Theme
color=.../>` seeds the brand colour the whole Material palette derives from, and
`<Styles/>` registers the named style rules in `templates/Styles.bsx`.

The infra commands (`deploy`, `sync`, the validate/plan/apply/destroy IaC verbs)
live on the workspace root entry's `<BeetSiteDeployHost>`, so this entry stays
purely the served site.
-->
<StartOnLoad {(HttpServer, TuiServer, SshTuiServer)}>
<Router {(RequestLogger, AnalyticsMiddleware, AnalyticsConfig, CacheHeadersMiddleware, CacheHeaders, HelpHandler, NavigateHandler, BsxLayout{template:"Layout"})}>
	<!-- `binary_name` is the cloud resource prefix, so it must be the deploy's
	     stack app name (`beet-site`), NOT the generic `beet` binary this site
	     runs on: it is what names the analytics table at runtime. -->
	<PackageConfig title="Beet" binary_name="beet-site" description="The beet website, built with beet" version="0.0.9-dev.16"/>
	<Theme color={Srgba(Srgba{red:0.0, green:1.0, blue:0.75, alpha:1.0})}/>
	<TemplateDir src="templates"/>
	<Styles/>
	<DefaultAppRoutes/>
	<RoutesDir src="routes"/>
	<AssetsDir src="assets" cache="1h"/>
</Router>
</StartOnLoad>
